{"id": "EUVD-2026-99245", "enisaUuid": "192319c7-a1fc-31e5-9ad1-f67cf95a0f7c", "description": "Roo Code through 3.54.0 contains a command approval bypass vulnerability that allows attackers to run denied shell commands because parseCommandLine() treats ${ command; } substitutions as parameter expansions. Attackers using indirect prompt injection can embed denied commands inside an allowlisted command like echo to execute them without user approval on bash 5.3+ or ksh93.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T18:49:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T19:34:25", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/7rah/oss-cve/blob/6adb836d24ca446fd168c3acdc4c170beb77fe0f/roocode-group03-funsub.md", "https://github.com/RooCodeInc/Roo-Code/blob/v3.54.0/src/shared/parse-command.ts#L74-L79", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/roo-code-through-3.54.0-auto-approve-bypass-via-funsub-command-substitution"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110204", "GHSA-mfc9-vhw7-f5w9"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.51, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "79530acd-829a-303e-8c59-99d8185a9943", "product": {"name": "Roo-Code", "vendor": {"name": "RooCodeInc"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.54.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "943fb13e-7e57-39ac-8f12-6ba9b174c308", "vendor": {"name": "RooCodeInc"}}], "isExploited": false}